From b1e67d5fb21141989f854af01bebe618e1d0e457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 15:25:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Plan C-1 v5 mode H: fix canon-2input no-op comment (FALSIFIED
 by D2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The prior comment in lut_apply_with_canon claimed the canon-2input layer is
"empirically a no-op at pin-friendly columns". Cyclone_CRAM_Mapper deliverable
D2 (canon_2input_codec_table_d1pp.json) FALSIFIED that: canon-2input is a real
per-position XOR delta of 17-66 cells. The consumer byte-identity gate
docs/analysis/mode_h_canon/test_canon_vs_golden.py reconstructs the Quartus
golds 0/44 without canon, 44/44 with it.

Comment-only correction. The σ⁻¹-only code path is unchanged and remains
correct for the shipped symmetric scope {0x0000,0xFFFF}: at runtime the LE
reads only its 16 LUT data cells (H1, silicon-validated @ (22,12,4)
2026-05-21), so canon cells Quartus would emit are fitter metadata, not
load-bearing. Asymmetric masks require a host-prepared .rbf and remain gated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.c b/sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.c
index a1d97e2..09f8f6d 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/lutcodec.c
@@ -118,11 +118,22 @@ lc_status_t lut_apply_with_canon(uint8_t *rbf,
     lut_codec_t lc;
     lc_status_t st = lc_init(&lc, x, y, n);
     if (st != LC_OK) return st;
-    /* canon-2input asymmetric-mask layer is empirically a no-op at
-     * pin-friendly columns (Quartus emission matches zero-baseline
-     * canon state).  When this port is extended to X∈{3,4,6,7}
-     * (left-edge), apply the appropriate CANON_2INPUT_ABSOLUTE
-     * transition cells here before lut_apply_mask. */
+    /* IMPORTANT (2026-05-31): the canon-2input layer is NOT a no-op — that
+     * earlier claim was FALSIFIED by Cyclone_CRAM_Mapper D2
+     * (canon_2input_codec_table_d1pp.json): it is a real per-position XOR
+     * delta of 17-66 cells (lab_cram + block_band). The consumer byte-identity
+     * gate (docs/analysis/mode_h_canon/test_canon_vs_golden.py) reconstructs
+     * the Quartus golds 0/44 without canon, 44/44 with it.
+     *
+     * This path INTENTIONALLY applies σ⁻¹ ONLY, because:
+     *   (a) for the symmetric scope {0x0000,0xFFFF} that mode H ships,
+     *       σ⁻¹-only is silicon-validated (mode H @ (22,12,4), 2026-05-21):
+     *       the runtime LE reads only its 16 LUT data cells (H1), so the canon
+     *       cells Quartus would emit are fitter metadata, not load-bearing; and
+     *   (b) the 246 KB canon table cannot fit on-chip.
+     * Asymmetric masks therefore require a HOST-prepared .rbf (σ⁻¹+canon
+     * applied on the host, mode H only stages it) and remain gated — see
+     * docs/analysis/mode_h_canon/README.md. Do NOT apply canon on-chip here. */
     lut_apply_mask(rbf, &lc, mask, dirty);
     return LC_OK;
 }
